# Redirects the docs.overture.bio build publishes.
#
# Six of them, all for the same reason. While the marketing pages were being
# ported they were part of this build and public on this host, at /home/,
# /products/, /impact/, /collaborate/, /privacy/ and /terms-conditions/. The
# split moved them to overture.bio and they no longer exist here, so each one
# points at its new address cross-host.
#
# No force: these paths do not exist in this build, and Netlify applies a
# redirect when nothing else matches. Forcing would mask a future docs page at
# one of these paths.
#
# Netlify combines these with any rules configured in the site's UI; the UI
# rules are applied first.

/home/*              https://overture.bio/                    301
/products/*          https://overture.bio/products/           301
/impact/*            https://overture.bio/impact/             301
/collaborate/*       https://overture.bio/collaborate/        301
/privacy/*           https://overture.bio/privacy/            301
/terms-conditions/*  https://overture.bio/terms-conditions/   301
